  "base_commit": "5489a532e65ee3f5ab0959ff8a5da346ced96f2a",
  "pr_number": 6553,
  "issue_number": 6550,
  "issue_title": "`toJSONSchema()`: chaining `.int()` after `.min()`/`.max()` replaces explicit bounds",
  "issue_body": "Calling `.int()` after explicit numeric constraints changes the generated JSON Schema, even though runtime validation behaves identically.\n\nTested with:\n\n- Zod 4.5.4\n- Node.js 24.18.0\n- JSON Schema Draft 2020-12 and OpenAPI 3.0 targets\n\n### Minimal reproduction\n\n```ts\nimport * as z from \"zod\";\n\nconst intFirst = z.number().int().min(0).max(23);\nconst intLast = z.number().min(0).max(23).int();\n\nfor (const target of [\"draft-2020-12\", \"openapi-3.0\"] as const) {\n  console.log(target);\n  console.log(\"intFirst\", z.toJSONSchema(intFirst, { target }));\n  console.log(\"intLast\", z.toJSONSchema(intLast, { target }));\n}\n```\n\n### Actual output\n\nFor both targets:\n\n```ts\n// z.number().int().min(0).max(23)\n{\n  type: \"integer\",\n  minimum: 0,\n  maximum: 23\n}\n\n// z.number().min(0).max(23).int()\n{\n  type: \"integer\",\n  minimum: -9007199254740991,\n  maximum: 9007199254740991\n}\n```\n\nBoth schemas still behave identically during runtime validation:\n\n- `-1` is rejected\n- `0` is accepted\n- `1.5` is rejected\n- `23` is accepted\n- `24` is rejected\n\n### Expected output\n\nThe explicit `minimum: 0` and `maximum: 23` constraints should be preserved regardless of whether `.int()` appears before or after them.\n\nAt minimum, the generated schema should not describe different accepted ranges when the two Zod schemas accept the same values.\n\nThis matters when `toJSONSchema()` is used to produce an OpenAPI contract: applying `.int()` last causes the published contract to lose the application's explicit range.\n\n### Related issue\n\n[#4779](https://github.com/colinhacks/zod/issues/4779) discusses the default safe-integer range emitted for an unconstrained integer. This case is different because explicit, tighter constraints are present and enforced at runtime, but are replaced only in the generated schema when `.int()` is applied last.\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-09-02T20:45:59Z",
